// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Undying Loyalty
// @category Friendship / Loyalty
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Undying_Loyalty
// @domain   Narrative
// @scale    arc
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): a character defined by unwavering loyalty — faithful to a person or cause through
// every hardship, when anyone else would abandon them. FRONTIER: loyalty as the defining, unbreakable
// trait. The discriminator is a [+Steadfast] character bound on the agent of a [&StandsBy] event toward the
// one they will not forsake — devotion proven at cost. Distinct from a mere ally (loyalty of convenience) by
// the through-anything constancy, and from Conflicting Loyalty (a loyalty torn) by its singleness.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc undying_loyalty -> [
  i_gave_my_word : "the standing-trait form of",
  power_of_friendship : "the constancy that fuels",
  conflicting_loyalty : "the undivided opposite of"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the through-anything faithful one is the discriminator; promotion model) —
prop Steadfast [+Social]            // unwavering in loyalty — faithful through any hardship, when others would quit
verb StandsBy(other) [+Interpersonal] // remains loyal to another at great cost, refusing to abandon them

imply UndyingLoyalty -> [Devotion, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (arc scale): a [+Steadfast] character STANDS BY another — the faithful one bound on the agent
// role of a [&StandsBy] event (other=$liege), so phase-2 re-checks [+Steadfast] on the loyal one (STYLE §8).
// Binding the through-anything constancy on the one who refuses to abandon is the discriminator: loyalty as
// the unbreakable defining trait, parting it from an ally of convenience and from a divided, conflicted loyalty.
rule Undying_Loyalty {
  when:
    char $loyal [+Steadfast]
    char $liege
    $loyal != $liege
    evt  $devotion [&StandsBy(agent=$loyal, other=$liege)]
  then:
    $devotion [+UndyingLoyalty]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: The Lord of the Rings — Samwise Gamgee (novel/film) ===
// Sam follows Frodo out of the Shire and never once turns back. Through Moria, through Shelob's lair, through
// the ash of Mordor where the quest grinds them both to ruin, he carries the food, the gear, the hope — and
// at the last, on the slopes of Mount Doom when Frodo can go no further, he carries Frodo himself: "I can't
// carry it for you, but I can carry you!" No hardship breaks him; no horror makes him leave. The truest
// undying loyalty in the canon.

// SAMWISE GAMGEE — faithful to Frodo through Mordor and beyond, who will not abandon him
char sam [+Steadfast] [+Protagonist]

// FRODO BAGGINS — the one he will not forsake, carried at the last
char frodo [+Protagonist]

// EXT. MOUNT DOOM - the ash slopes, the end of the road
set mount_doom [+Exterior]

scene the_slopes {
  beat 1 {
    sam @ mount_doom
    frodo @ mount_doom
    // when Frodo can go no further, Sam carries him — loyalty no horror could break
    evt the_carrying [&StandsBy(agent=sam, other=frodo)]
    // Undying_Loyalty -> the_carrying [+UndyingLoyalty]
  }
}
